5. Nc3 fxe4 { With a knight on c3, the exchange now suits Black: dxe4 leaves White no centre pawn on d3 to guard, and the f-file is open. } 6. dxe4 ( 6. Nxe4 $2 { Takes with the knight, but then the black pawn forks it. } 6... d5 { Hits the bishop on c4 and the knight on e4 together. } 7. Nxf6+ gxf6 8. Bb3 Rg8 { The pawns are doubled but the g-file and the centre are Black's. } ) 6... Bb4 { Pins the knight on c3 to the king, which takes away the main guard of e4 and d5. } 7. O-O Bxc3 { Trades the bishop to double White's pawns. After bxc3 the pawn on e4 is weak. } 8. bxc3 d6 { Supports e5 and develops the c8 bishop. White has the bishop pair, so keep the position closed. } 9. a4 Qe7 { Develops and watches e4 and a3. The game is roughly level. Plan: castle long or short, then hit e4 with ...Nd7-c5 or ...Bg4. } *
